{"meta":{"format_version":"5.0","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"wall_softwood","model_identifier":"wall_softwood","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","multi_file_ruleset":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"# wall_softwood\n\nSoftwood wall: a straight segment one column (16 u) long along X, outer face toward -Z. End caps at both ends meet the next segment's cap to form a joint post. Timber (pale, rough, rope-lashed softwood logs), 3 m (106 u) with pointed tops and a fighting step behind at 78 u.\n\n- Footprint: 1 x 1 columns (16 x 16 units, 0.45 x 0.45 m), centred on the origin, front (door side) faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -8..8, y 0..109, z -7..8 units.\n- Texture: 128 x 128, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering, flat pixel-art tones per material (repainted in Patch 5 for colour contrast).\n- Cubes: finished 14, construction_0 19, construction_33 23, construction_66 27, ruined 28 (the state sets are cut from the finished cubes and map into the texture regions of the faces they were cut from).\n\n## State group sets (children of `root`; show exactly one)\n\n- `finished`: the finished building (visible by default).\n- `construction_0`, `construction_33`, `construction_66`: build progress at 0 %, 33 % and 66 % (staked outline and footing with materials waiting, then walls rising inside scaffold).\n- `ruined`: broken walls at uneven heights, rubble and fallen beams.\n- `wall_softwood_damaged.png`: damaged texture (cracks, scorch) for the same UVs; works on every group set.\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 16 x 106 x 16 centred at x 0, z 2\n\n## Attachment and effect points (empty groups)\n\n- `slot_wall_walk` at (0, 78, 6)"},"resolution":{"width":128,"height":128},"elements":[{"name":"log_wall_log0#9a7a50","box_uv":false,"render_order":"default","locked":false,"export":true,"scope":0,"allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[-8,0,-6],"to":[-4,106,-2],"autouv":0,"color":0,"origin":[0,0